    <p>
      <strong>Proof.</strong>
      Proposition <a href="/tag/BC6285" data-tag="BC6285">2.4.4.2</a> implies that $p$ is fully faithful. If $Y$ is any object of $\calD $, then $Y$ is equivalent in the fiber $\calD _{q(Y)}$ to the image under $p$ of some vertex of $\calC _{q(Y)}$. Thus $p$ is essentially surjective and the proof is complete. 
      <span class="qed">$\square$</span>
    </p>
